WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.869
-Now, you both are sisters,
and you're obviously close,

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.771
but I wanted to see
just how close you are

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:07.706
in a game we like to call,
"Know Your Sis."

00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:08.941
Now, here's how it works.

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:11.443
One of you will wear
noise-canceling headphones

00:00:11.443 --> 00:00:14.014
while the other answers
a question about you.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.782
And then you'll
take the headphones off,

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.717
and we'll see
if your answer matches.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.218
Make sense?

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.386
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:21.887
-Charli, the first question
is about you,

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:24.423
so please put on
your headphones,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:26.960
Charli, and play
some music loud.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.563
Give a thumbs-up when you're
ready, and you can't hear us.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.566
Alright, Dixie,
here's the question.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.435
Ready?
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:42.174
-What is the most normal
teenager thing that Charli does?

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:46.579
-Um, her room basically
looks like a toy store

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:51.584
with stuffed animals,
kinetic sand, Orbeez.

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.988
Like, she has
a 5-year-old's room.

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:57.523
-Okay. Okay.

00:00:57.523 --> 00:00:58.658
Wow.
-That's what she would say.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:01.160
-Okay. Here we go.
Alright, good.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.063
The question was, "What's
the most normal teenager thing

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.598
that Charli does?"

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:09.201
-Um, probably the fact
that I have a lot of toys,

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:10.836
which is probably the --
[ Bell rings ]

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:13.039
-That matches!

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:15.240
We have one point there.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.278
You just -- That's just normal.
You just love toys.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.312
-She tells me all the time.

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:23.583
She's like, "You're very normal.
Like, it's weird."

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.317
-Like, yeah. Alright, Dixie,

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:26.586
your turn to
put on the headphones

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.689
and give us a thumbs-up
when you can't hear us.

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:34.961
Okay. Here we go.

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.629
Charli, here's the question.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:37.797
-Okay.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:42.902
-What is Dixie most likely to do
on a day off?

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.804
-Take a nap for the entire day.

00:01:45.804 --> 00:01:47.373
-Really? Like, how --

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.407
-Yeah.

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:50.643
-Like how long? Like, an hour?

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.211
Couple hours?
-Like the whole day.

00:01:52.211 --> 00:01:55.548
-The whole day.
-Like a solid five, eight hours.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.050
-Really?

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.451
-Yeah.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.587
-Wowzers!
Alright, that's interesting.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.323
Alright. Let me ask Dixie. Okay.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.894
-Hi. [ Chuckling ] I'm scared.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.928
-Dixie, here's the question.

00:02:09.928 --> 00:02:15.635
"What does Dixie most likely do
on a day off?"

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:16.970
-Probably sleep all day

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.904
and watch like Netflix
or something.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.406
[ Bell dings ]
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.907
You guys know each other well!

00:02:21.907 --> 00:02:23.175
This is exactly right.

00:02:23.175 --> 00:02:24.711
Okay, for the final round,

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.412
Dixie, please
put on the headphones,

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:29.115
give us a thumbs-up
when you can't hear us.

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:31.851
[ Chuckling ] Charli,
here's the question. Ready?

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.320
"When is a time
that Dixie broke the rules

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.124
that your parents
still don't know about?"

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:40.526
Come on.
-I'm gonna get her in trouble.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:43.329
She stole my mom's car once.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.197
-[ Gasps ]
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.100
I don't want
to get her in trouble.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.102
Sorry, Mom.
-Wait, where did --

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.738
What are you talking about?
Where did she go?

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.072
-I don't know.
She probably went to,

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.141
like, a friend's house
or something.

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:58.111
I think she just wanted
to be, like, rebellious once,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.312
and that was it.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.612
She stopped there.

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:03.015
-Was it late at night?

00:03:03.015 --> 00:03:05.118
-I have no idea.
I just remember her telling me,

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:06.819
like, "Oh, yeah,
I stole the car."

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:07.987
I was like, "Okay!"

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:10.223
-Does Mom know about this?

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:12.725
-I don't think so.

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:16.696
I hope she does, though, so
I'm not the person to tell her.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.897
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.699
-Okay, very good.
Let's have Dixie take off the --

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.501
-Am I good? Good?

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.735
-Screaming.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:25.103
-Oh, am I loud?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.103 --> 00:03:27.373
-Dixie, the question was,

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.875
"When was a time
that you broke the rules

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.412
that your parents
still don't know about?"

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.413
-Watch her expose herself
for something else.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.849
[ Laughs ]
-It might happen.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:41.221
-That my parents
still don't know about?

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:46.025
Um...

00:03:46.025 --> 00:03:47.693
-Did you sneak out?
-Okay, they know this.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.496
I literally just told them this
a couple weeks ago, though,

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:53.366
but I did steal my mom's car
in high school

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:54.900
to drive to my friend's house.
-Gosh.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.503
-That is correct!
Oh, you're so lucky!

00:03:57.503 --> 00:04:00.239
You're so lucky! I wanted
to hear the other story,

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:03.375
'cause you're like,
"Uh, which one?"

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:04.476
You lucked out.
-I was so nervous

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:05.744
she was gonna say
something else.

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:07.513
I was like,
we just revealed two things

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.648
that our parents
would not want to know.

00:04:09.648 --> 00:04:11.450
-That's what I was waiting for.
I go, oh, my God.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.419
Well, you got a good sister
right there.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:16.222
You guys are good --
Yeah, you're great sisters.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.258
Congrats on that.
That is "Know Your Sis."

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:22.662
"The D'Amelio Show"
is coming to Hulu this summer.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.896
Thanks so much
for being here, guys.

